cff-version: 1.2.0
title: NOVA course 2026 — point cloud tooling
message: >-
  If you use this software or its documentation, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: José M.
    family-names: Beltrán Abaunza
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences, Lund University, Sweden
    website: https://github.com/jobelab
repository-code: https://github.com/jobelab/nova-course-2026
abstract: >-
  Python reimplementation of a tree detection and segmentation workflow for
  terrestrial laser scanning point clouds: Cloth Simulation Filter ground
  classification, height normalisation, cross-section stem detection with a
  weighted verticality/reflectance screen, 3D Dijkstra region growing for tree
  instance labelling, and RANSAC stem taper reconstruction. Written as marimo
  notebooks and a small library, with every method scored against reference
  labels. Independent student work produced alongside the NOVA PhD course
  "Introduction to Point Cloud Processing for Forest Sciences".
keywords:
  - point cloud
  - terrestrial laser scanning
  - forest inventory
  - tree segmentation
  - instance segmentation
  - stem taper
  - LiDAR
  - open science
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
date-released: '2026-08-20'
